# System information\n\nGodot v4.6.2.stable (001aa128b) - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Tue, 21 Apr 2026 23:38:22 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 Laptop GPU - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-11800H @ 2.30GHz (16 threads) - 15.35 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen a `TabContainer` node has one or multiple children, the appear as part of the `TabContainer` in the inspector. There you can set these individual tabs as `disabled` and/or `hidden`, neither of which work when the project is exported.\n\nWhen running the project in-editor, they are correctly hidden and disabled\n\nAdditionally, when getting the data of whether a tab is or isn't hidden and/or disabled, depending on what script does it, the output is different when running in editor. If the script is *on* the `TabContainer` node itself, they *always* report those options are set to `false`, when higher up, they report it correctly, but only when running in editor.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a scene with a `TabContainer` and at least one child\n2. Set the tab to `hidden` and/or `disabled`\n3. Make sure it is hidden and/or disabled by running the project in editor (not web)\n4. Export the project and run the exported project\n5. Observe that the tabs you set as `hidden` and/or `disabled` are in fact not `hidden` and/or `disabled`\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27101890/mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_u